      "lineNbr": 320,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T21:51:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We cannot quite.  peek_c is how many bytes from the queue has been \"peeked at\", that is placed into rx_buffer[] without being removed from the queue.  There could be more bytes in the buffer than indicated by peek_c, and in this case, we need to know if there are at least 6 bytes, but peek_c is currently capped at 5 (the number that we need to be sure that we can decode the length of a I2C request.)",
      "parentUuid": "dd722a5a_82d30d2b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 320,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "1bef08d3dccdffc82140e219cf063c011a5c8d7b",
