      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T21:51:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unlike `udelay()`, `usleep()` which is used here will put the current EC task into sleep state, and invoke the scheduler to process other tasks while waiting.\n\nI have verified that the EC console remains response even while this code is sitting in `usleep()`.\n\nHonestly though, I am not sure which task is running the methods scheduled with `hook_call_deferred()` (which is how this runs), nor whether it is frowned upon to put that task into a timed sleep (possibly holding up other deferred calls.)\n\nTo be sure not to cause any unduly delay to other hook handlers, I have created a new separate EC task for these JTAG routines.",
      "parentUuid": "54e4b274_4b541042",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 334,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 334,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "1bef08d3dccdffc82140e219cf063c011a5c8d7b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
