        "uuid": "48da55c5_390e3b17",
        "filename": "board/hyperdebug/cmsis-dap.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 432,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T19:30:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why kind of delays are possible here. This looks like another watchdog potential",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 431,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 432,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "1bef08d3dccdffc82140e219cf063c011a5c8d7b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d07da91_78b93f24",
        "filename": "board/hyperdebug/cmsis-dap.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 432,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T21:51:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a 16-bit counter, and the maximum value we use for starting the countdown is 32767 (see `dap_swj_clock()`).  At 104Mhz core clock frequency, that means that we can at most wait around 315μs here.  This method is called from within the bit-banging logic of `dap_jtag_sequence()`.\n\nReading the CMSIS-DAP protocol, one could think that 255 sequences each of 64 clock cycles could be requested at once, (this request would be almost 2kB of USB data, more than our queues support), but I have seen OpenOCD break up requests, so that they are no longer than 5 sequences of 64 clock cycles, plus a few one-clock sequences.  This would limit the time spent in one invocation of `dap_jtag_sequence()` to about 200ms.  I have tried artificially running the clock as slow as possible, and seen that the requests sent by OpenOCD can be handled by HyperDebug in 207ms without triggering watchdog issues.",
      "parentUuid": "48da55c5_390e3b17",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 431,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 432,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "1bef08d3dccdffc82140e219cf063c011a5c8d7b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
